00:21:21.859 --> 00:21:24.490
It's funny.

00:21:24.490 --> 00:21:27.490
When doing what you think is right for someone, it can feel so...

00:21:27.490 --> 00:21:33.750
wrong.

00:21:33.750 --> 00:21:34.750
How about you and this guy?

00:21:34.750 --> 00:21:38.410
Well, Clark.

00:21:38.410 --> 00:21:39.410
I'm every guy's as nice as you.

00:21:39.410 --> 00:21:43.819
I had to get Adam away from him.

00:21:43.819 --> 00:21:45.819
I'm sorry.

00:21:46.819 --> 00:21:47.819
Does he know where you are?

00:21:47.819 --> 00:21:56.039
I changed my name so he couldn't find us.

00:21:56.039 --> 00:22:01.039
I had so much I was fighting for, trying to change the world.

00:22:01.039 --> 00:22:04.039
And now I have to hide behind the power of the pen in a new name,

00:22:04.039 --> 00:22:08.039
making sure nobody knows who's behind the words I'm printing.

00:22:08.039 --> 00:22:10.039
Kind of like the vigilantes.

00:22:10.039 --> 00:22:18.839
Must have been scary escaping from him.

00:22:18.839 --> 00:22:20.839
All I know is I protected my son.

00:22:20.839 --> 00:22:25.180
You know the world may never see me as some big hero.

00:22:25.180 --> 00:22:31.079
Maybe someday my son will.

00:22:31.079 --> 00:22:44.180
What about the green arrow in those first?

00:22:44.180 --> 00:22:46.180
that try to blow me up, they know where I am.

00:22:46.180 --> 00:22:49.180
Just stay here, you'll be safe. I'll be back. I promise.

00:22:49.180 --> 00:23:04.259
It feels like somehow I was destined to be with Clark, but his destiny is so much bigger.

00:23:04.259 --> 00:23:09.259
And the last thing that I would ever want is to be the one thing that holds him back or stands in the way.

00:23:09.259 --> 00:23:13.259
And what if you're exactly the thing that might help him be the person you know he can be?

00:23:13.259 --> 00:23:16.259
What if you're the one who makes his burden easier to bear?

00:23:16.259 --> 00:23:19.599
Do you think that's why he sent you?

00:23:19.599 --> 00:23:22.599
To make sure I was safe?

00:23:22.599 --> 00:23:24.599
He worries about you.

00:23:24.599 --> 00:23:28.599
He still thinks you don't know about his powers.

00:23:28.599 --> 00:23:32.599
See, that's another reason for me to be here.

00:23:32.599 --> 00:23:36.079
When it comes to big secrets, I'm not exactly Matahari.

00:23:36.079 --> 00:23:38.079
I could blow it all for him.

00:23:38.079 --> 00:23:41.079
With every great relationship, Lois,

00:23:41.079 --> 00:23:46.859
comes a great burden and the strength to carry it.

00:23:46.859 --> 00:23:52.000
Okay.

00:23:52.000 --> 00:23:55.000
Well, I better get my beauty sleep.

00:23:55.000 --> 00:23:59.910
All this dry heat.

00:23:59.910 --> 00:24:11.140
Lois, I'd like you to have something that was given to me by my wife.

00:24:11.140 --> 00:24:16.140
wife. It's a story about two star-crossed lovers.

00:24:16.140 --> 00:24:20.140
Prince Kufu and Shirea were murdered by an evil man, but

00:24:20.140 --> 00:24:27.150
their love was so strong they were bonded for all eternity.

00:24:27.150 --> 00:24:34.680
Lifetime after lifetime they were reborn to find their one true love,

00:24:34.680 --> 00:24:36.680
only to lose each other in death again.

00:24:36.680 --> 00:24:45.359
It's a terrible story.

00:24:45.359 --> 00:24:47.710
I like it.

00:24:47.710 --> 00:24:50.710
If you're into the whole Egyptian Groundhog Day thing.

00:24:50.710 --> 00:24:53.710
After many years, Kufu grew tired of always waiting to find his belief.

00:24:53.710 --> 00:24:57.470
waiting to find his beloved.

00:24:57.470 --> 00:24:59.470
So he traveled the world,

00:24:59.470 --> 00:25:01.470
seeking other women,

00:25:01.470 --> 00:25:03.470
trying to forget Shai'era.

00:25:03.470 --> 00:25:09.119
Unable to rid her from his heart,

00:25:09.119 --> 00:25:11.119
he returned home, resigned to his fate.

00:25:11.119 --> 00:25:14.809
No sooner did he arrive at the palace

00:25:14.809 --> 00:25:17.809
when he saw her.

00:25:17.809 --> 00:25:25.440
She was there all along, but he didn't recognize her

00:25:25.440 --> 00:25:27.440
because the time wasn't right.

00:25:27.440 --> 00:25:36.970
He needed to wait because it made their love stronger

00:25:36.970 --> 00:25:44.730
and their kiss that much sweeter.

00:25:44.730 --> 00:25:53.549
Try that again, and the next thing,

00:25:53.549 --> 00:25:54.549
kissing your lips will be my fist.

00:25:54.549 --> 00:26:09.079
I had Luther Corp's ballistic people up all night taking apart that slug from Kat's car.

00:26:09.079 --> 00:26:10.079
I appreciate that, thanks.

00:26:10.079 --> 00:26:13.079
I'm not asking for your thanks, Clark.

00:26:13.079 --> 00:26:15.079
Just your trust.

00:26:15.079 --> 00:26:16.079
You need me.

00:26:16.079 --> 00:26:20.000
You said this was urgent.

00:26:20.000 --> 00:26:23.000
After the lab techs pulled apart the bullet and reassembled it,

00:26:23.000 --> 00:26:32.559
they found this.

00:26:32.559 --> 00:26:33.559
Target is me.

00:26:33.559 --> 00:26:36.559
Guess our assassin never was after Hello Kitty.

00:26:36.559 --> 00:26:42.400
This guy doesn't know that car explosions and bullets don't hurt me.

00:26:42.400 --> 00:26:45.400
It's possible. He's just testing you to see what you're made of.

00:26:45.400 --> 00:26:46.400
what you're made of.

00:26:46.400 --> 00:26:48.400
Why hasn't he come after me again?

00:26:48.400 --> 00:26:50.400
Maybe he didn't realize how difficult of a target you are.

00:26:50.400 --> 00:26:52.400
This guy never gives up.

00:26:52.400 --> 00:26:54.400
And he gets every detail right.

00:26:54.400 --> 00:26:56.400
It must be more to his plan.

00:26:56.400 --> 00:26:58.400
If he knows you're faster than his bullets,

00:26:58.400 --> 00:27:02.400
the only place to aim is at someone he knows you'll save.

00:27:02.400 --> 00:27:05.400
And maybe you'll be there to...

00:27:05.400 --> 00:27:07.400
Act as a shield.

00:27:07.400 --> 00:27:11.400
It's Cat. I have to get back to Small Hill.

00:27:11.400 --> 00:27:13.400
Too late.

00:27:13.400 --> 00:27:14.400
Our kitten reporter's already on the move.

00:27:14.400 --> 00:27:15.400
is already on the move.

00:27:15.400 --> 00:27:25.400
Pack up Adams things and have him ready.

00:27:25.400 --> 00:27:27.400
Some is after me, and he may know about us.

00:27:27.400 --> 00:27:29.400
I liked you better, Isabloom.

00:27:29.400 --> 00:27:57.769
Why are you doing this to me?

00:27:57.769 --> 00:27:59.769
I didn't do anything.

00:27:59.769 --> 00:28:01.769
Funny thing about fate.

00:28:01.769 --> 00:28:03.769
You can't outrun it.

00:28:03.769 --> 00:28:09.880
Either it's your day or it's not, sweet pee.

00:28:09.880 --> 00:28:12.880
Please, no.

00:28:12.880 --> 00:28:17.190
My son, she's just two years old.

00:28:17.190 --> 00:28:20.980
I'm all he's got.

00:28:20.980 --> 00:28:22.980
Trust me.

00:28:22.980 --> 00:28:24.980
He'll get over you.

00:28:24.980 --> 00:28:28.980
Three or four years, he won't even remember your face.

00:28:28.980 --> 00:28:34.980
People about to die always think that that special loved one won't be able to go on without them.

00:28:34.980 --> 00:28:40.980
But the truth is, that person just finds someone else to love.

00:28:40.980 --> 00:28:43.980
Everyone is replaceable.

00:28:43.980 --> 00:28:48.980
I used to think everyone could be saved, even those superhero freaks.

00:28:48.980 --> 00:28:53.980
But now I realize some people are just born dead.

00:28:53.980 --> 00:30:30.339
I was so brave.

00:30:30.339 --> 00:30:33.230
Are you okay?

00:30:33.230 --> 00:30:37.559
I'm fine.

00:30:37.559 --> 00:30:41.029
Thanks to my bulletproof vest.

00:30:41.029 --> 00:30:45.809
Don't leave home without it, Clark Kent.

00:30:45.809 --> 00:30:48.809
You can never be too safe.

00:30:48.809 --> 00:30:50.809
Well, I'll be sure to pick one up.

00:30:50.809 --> 00:30:53.809
See, I don't need a mask hero to rescue me.

00:30:53.809 --> 00:30:58.920
I've got a real flesh and blood one right here.

00:30:58.920 --> 00:31:04.150
People need to see someone's heart to believe in them.

00:31:04.150 --> 00:31:10.710
We need to be inspired by people who stand out in the light.

00:31:10.710 --> 00:31:13.710
Not people who shrink into the shadows.

00:31:13.710 --> 00:31:16.710
We need a good old American hero in red, white, and blue.

00:31:16.710 --> 00:31:22.869
Or at least red and blue.

00:31:22.869 --> 00:32:26.369
Did you miss me?

00:32:26.369 --> 00:32:29.369
I got to say, we had something special.

00:32:29.369 --> 00:32:31.369
You didn't crack on the first beating.

00:32:31.369 --> 00:32:33.369
It made me work for it.

00:32:33.369 --> 00:32:37.099
I'm glad it was good for you, too.

00:32:37.099 --> 00:32:39.099
You get easy there, Commando.

00:32:39.099 --> 00:32:42.099
I'm just a guy over here with bow and arrow.

00:32:42.099 --> 00:32:44.099
You're wasting your talent, Queen.

00:32:44.099 --> 00:32:47.099
You could make a real difference out there.

00:32:47.099 --> 00:32:49.099
Tide is turning.

00:32:49.099 --> 00:32:53.099
People are getting nervous about vigilantes roaming the streets.

00:32:53.099 --> 00:32:58.099
taking the decisions and the glory out of the hands of the suits in power.

00:32:58.099 --> 00:32:59.099
I'm not running for office.

00:32:59.099 --> 00:33:01.099
I'm just putting bad guys in jail.

00:33:01.099 --> 00:33:02.099
It's going to get tougher the longer.

00:33:02.099 --> 00:33:05.099
You and your little league of heroes stay half in, half out.

00:33:05.099 --> 00:33:07.099
That's the beauty of my group.

00:33:07.099 --> 00:33:10.099
Everybody thinks we're dead.

00:33:10.099 --> 00:33:14.980
We could use you.

00:33:14.980 --> 00:33:16.980
But this is your one and only offer.

00:33:16.980 --> 00:33:19.980
You raise a good point.

00:33:19.980 --> 00:33:30.839
On the other hand, you did just shoot me.

00:33:30.839 --> 00:33:36.869
Where's...

00:33:36.869 --> 00:33:38.869
Chloe Solomon? Where is she?

00:33:38.869 --> 00:33:41.690
I'm sorry.

00:33:41.690 --> 00:33:43.690
I can't hear you.

00:33:43.690 --> 00:33:46.690
Where is Chloe?

00:33:46.690 --> 00:33:53.559
It wasn't a kidnapping.

00:33:53.559 --> 00:33:55.559
It was a trade.

00:33:55.559 --> 00:33:59.680
Trade for what?

00:33:59.680 --> 00:34:00.680
You!

00:34:00.680 --> 00:34:06.640
She didn't crack.

00:34:06.640 --> 00:34:10.639
She downed a cyanide pill just to save your life.

00:34:10.639 --> 00:34:50.719
Chloe is gone.

00:34:50.719 --> 00:34:53.719
What do you mean?

00:34:53.719 --> 00:34:56.719
Those people who are holding me at that old brewery.

00:34:56.719 --> 00:34:58.719
She traded herself in so I just

00:34:58.719 --> 00:35:00.719
She traded herself in so I could be free.

00:35:00.719 --> 00:35:05.860
Who are these people? What do they want with Chloe?

00:35:05.860 --> 00:35:09.860
Just a group of people that call themselves crime fighters.

00:35:09.860 --> 00:35:12.860
They think we should all remain hidden in the shadows.

00:35:12.860 --> 00:35:16.869
I tried to torture her.

00:35:16.869 --> 00:35:23.010
Clark. She beat them at their own game. She took a cyanide pill.

00:35:23.010 --> 00:35:25.010
No, Chloe wouldn't.

00:35:25.010 --> 00:35:27.010
Then she took this.

00:35:27.010 --> 00:35:29.010
I found that at her apartment.

00:35:29.010 --> 00:35:32.010
I had it tested, and there's

00:35:32.010 --> 00:35:38.210
traces of a cyanide antidote in there.

00:35:38.210 --> 00:35:39.210
She faked her own death.

00:35:39.210 --> 00:35:45.780
There's planning.

00:35:45.780 --> 00:35:48.699
ago.

00:35:48.699 --> 00:35:51.949
She saw the future.

00:35:51.949 --> 00:35:56.949
She put on Dr. Fait's helmet trying to find you and said it was going to be okay.

00:35:56.949 --> 00:35:58.949
Just let her go?

00:35:58.949 --> 00:36:00.949
I had no idea she was leaving.

00:36:00.949 --> 00:36:01.949
She put on the fate helmet, Clark.

00:36:01.949 --> 00:36:03.949
That should have told you something.

00:36:03.949 --> 00:36:05.949
Look, I understand how much she means to you, Oliver.

00:36:05.949 --> 00:36:07.949
But for years she's been asking us to treat her as one of us.

00:36:07.949 --> 00:36:11.949
She begged me to trust her and the decisions that she made.

00:36:11.949 --> 00:36:15.949
If she put this much planning and thought into leaving, she knew what she was doing.

00:36:15.949 --> 00:36:16.949
I go out to every night.

00:36:16.949 --> 00:36:17.949
I protect unfamiliar faces so that they can do.

00:36:17.949 --> 00:36:20.949
so that they can go home and be with the people that they care about.

00:36:20.949 --> 00:36:29.480
The one person that I should have been protecting the most...

00:36:29.480 --> 00:36:30.480
Failed her.

00:36:30.480 --> 00:36:33.480
We didn't choose this. We both know this is what we were born to do.

00:36:33.480 --> 00:36:35.480
Playing the fate card. Is that what you're doing again?

00:36:35.480 --> 00:36:37.480
That's what gets you through the day?

00:36:37.480 --> 00:36:39.480
You sit around and do nothing while these people that we protect,

00:36:39.480 --> 00:36:41.480
they paint us as vigilantes, Clark.

00:36:41.480 --> 00:36:43.480
The woman that you love ran away!

00:36:43.480 --> 00:36:45.480
You think I don't want to go get Lois and bring her back?

00:36:45.480 --> 00:36:51.489
They left us, Oliver.

00:36:51.489 --> 00:36:53.489
With our lives, we can't blame them.

00:36:53.489 --> 00:37:00.389
But what if we hadn't remain hidden?

00:37:00.389 --> 00:37:01.389
What if we didn't put our idea?

00:37:01.389 --> 00:37:03.389
out there to be held hostage.

00:37:03.389 --> 00:37:05.389
Would this still be happening?

00:37:05.389 --> 00:37:10.500
I think we have to forge new fate here.

00:37:10.500 --> 00:37:12.500
We've lost way too much.

00:37:12.500 --> 00:37:17.369
Something's got to change.

00:37:17.369 --> 00:37:43.280
Not even hello.

00:37:43.280 --> 00:37:48.000
Rotting in jail ain't my idea of a good time.

00:37:48.000 --> 00:37:52.949
You're a drop.

00:37:52.949 --> 00:38:00.960
You nailed your target.

00:38:00.960 --> 00:38:02.960
Now let's get you out of here.

00:38:02.960 --> 00:38:11.360
About time.

00:38:11.360 --> 00:38:14.360
I'm sorry. What's redneck for bite me?

00:38:14.360 --> 00:38:15.360
Plasty.

00:38:15.360 --> 00:38:18.360
Sir. Our costume counterparts are officially tagged and released.

00:38:18.360 --> 00:38:20.360
As soon as we spring wider,

00:38:20.360 --> 00:38:22.360
but over here, we can track their every move.

00:38:22.360 --> 00:38:27.360
Let's give these boys a taste of what it's like to mess on the suicide squad.

00:38:27.360 --> 00:38:37.039
Lois? About last night. I'm sorry.

00:38:37.039 --> 00:38:40.039
I guess I got a little too caught up in my story.

00:38:40.039 --> 00:38:43.039
You forgot to mention the most important part.

00:38:43.039 --> 00:38:46.039
It was an autobiography.

00:38:46.039 --> 00:38:50.059
I found this in the book.

00:38:50.059 --> 00:39:00.539
Lois, surely you don't think that...

00:39:00.539 --> 00:39:02.539
Let's just say I wasn't born yesterday.

00:39:02.539 --> 00:39:04.539
You're not the only one of Clark's friends.

00:39:04.539 --> 00:39:09.539
the only one of Clark's friends with a mysterious past.

00:39:09.539 --> 00:39:14.429
Clark did say you were wise beyond your years.

00:39:14.429 --> 00:39:17.429
I hope last night will remain between us.

00:39:17.429 --> 00:39:21.429
I'm not sure Clark would forgive me if he knew.

00:39:21.429 --> 00:39:26.280
Some leads are better left buried.

00:39:26.280 --> 00:39:29.280
So if you were just here to babysit me as a favorite of Clark,

00:39:29.280 --> 00:39:30.280
what was with the heart to heart?

00:39:30.280 --> 00:39:32.280
Something tells me that story time

00:39:32.280 --> 00:39:35.280
wasn't exactly part of the agreement.

00:39:35.280 --> 00:39:37.280
It's my wife.

00:39:37.280 --> 00:39:40.280
I've been hearing her in my thoughts,

00:39:40.280 --> 00:39:42.280
and last night I had a vision of her.

00:39:42.280 --> 00:39:47.280
When that happens, I know I'll be joining her soon in a new life.

00:39:47.280 --> 00:39:50.280
But to do that, I must first leave this one.

00:39:50.280 --> 00:39:54.280
Leave? Like, die?

00:39:54.280 --> 00:39:57.280
It's time I meet my destiny, Lois.

00:39:57.280 --> 00:40:03.269
But before I go, I wanted you to meet yours.

00:40:03.269 --> 00:40:08.469
You can't do it without you.

00:40:08.469 --> 00:40:10.469
You're his Shaiira.

00:40:10.469 --> 00:40:11.469
Carter, I am not like you.

00:40:11.469 --> 00:40:15.469
Carter, I am not like you and Shihira and Clark.

00:40:15.469 --> 00:40:24.420
My future is here in Africa.

00:40:24.420 --> 00:40:27.420
You know, the philosopher Nietzsche believed we shouldn't live for the future,

00:40:27.420 --> 00:40:28.420
but for the present.

00:40:28.420 --> 00:40:32.730
He thought that people who chased after some far-off future dream

00:40:32.730 --> 00:40:35.730
were really running away from their true destiny.

00:40:35.730 --> 00:40:39.199
Yeah, well, Nietzsche can call me a chicken if he wants,

00:40:39.199 --> 00:40:42.199
but he has never dated someone like Clark Kent.

00:40:42.199 --> 00:40:44.199
It wouldn't have mattered.

00:40:44.199 --> 00:40:47.199
To him, the true hero was the person who embraced the life

00:40:47.199 --> 00:40:49.199
that he or she was given and made it better.

00:40:49.199 --> 00:40:51.550
He called down.

00:40:51.550 --> 00:40:53.550
that person, Ubermich.

00:40:53.550 --> 00:40:58.969
A Superman.

00:40:58.969 --> 00:41:05.050
Nietzsche believed that all of us could be one in our own way.

